# When to use?
We can use git patches when we want to create a patch for specific versions of project and futhure will share this patch.

- it's better then PR because you can see how your commits will look like earlier;
- you can share your changes via email or file (target user doesn't have required permissions or two unconnected repos do not have common remote);
- during CI/CD for generating artifacts, automatic patches sending to email/teams/chat.


**Patch** - is a text represantation of changes between <start> and <end> commits. It includes:
- commit metadata (author, date, commit name, etc.);
- short and full description;
- changed files list;
- added and removed lines of the code.

It allows:
- Restore commit as it was originally created;
- Move patches between different branches and repos;
- Do Code Review easily by reading mails/files.

`git format-patch <start> <end>` file contains:

- `From <SHA> ...` - original commit hash
- Author and Date
- commit subject and commit body
- files list and changes stat
- `diff` with context
